aquinas-third-way.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: A1: "was" is taken as there could have been a time when nothing existed in A1 C1 and as there actually was a time when nothing existed where once_nothing is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C2 (S7) does not follow (aquinas-third-way.logic.r1.sense1)
aquinas-third-way.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C2 (S7): all_contingent = T, begin_needs_existing = T, nothing_now = F, once_nothing = F, once_nothing_2 = T
